# Angular feature folder structure

## Where code lives

- **Features:** `src/app/features/<feature-kebab>/` — all new UI and domain logic that belongs to one product area (e.g. `features/inventory/`).
- **Core:** `src/app/core/` — app-wide singletons only (auth session, API base URL, HTTP interceptors, global guards).
- **Shared:** `src/app/shared/` — reusable, feature-agnostic building blocks (dumb components, pipes, directives).

## Inside a feature

Colocate by responsibility:

- `components/` — presentational pieces used only in this feature
- `pages/` or `containers/` — routed views / smart containers
- `services/` — feature-scoped state and API calls
- `<feature>.routes.ts` — route definitions; load this file lazily from the root router
- Optional: `models/`, `data-access/` for types and API layers

## Data access responsibility (required)

- **Pages (`pages/` or `containers/`)** orchestrate data:
  - Read route params/query params.
  - Call **feature services** to load/save data.
  - Shape service results into view-model state and pass data down via `@Input()`.
  - Receive user intents via `@Output()` and decide what to do (call service, navigate, etc.).

- **Feature services (`services/`)** own API requests:
  - Contain all `HttpClient` usage and endpoint knowledge for the feature.
  - Centralize typing, mapping, and error handling for API interactions.

- **Presentational components (`components/`)** only preview/render:
  - Must not import/inject `HttpClient`, feature services, or route services.
  - Must not make API requests; emit events instead.

See also: `.cursor/rules/page-components-data-access.mdc`

## Routing

- Prefer **lazy loading**: `app.routes.ts` should reference `loadChildren` (or `loadComponent` chains) that point into `features/<name>/<feature>.routes.ts`, not list every child route inline in the root file.
- Feature route entry files should expose a **registration helper** and lazy pages via `loadComponent`. See: `.cursor/rules/feature-route-registration-lazy-load.mdc`

## Naming

- Folders and file names: **kebab-case** (Angular CLI default).
- Component selectors: keep the **`app`** prefix (project `prefix` in `angular.json`).

## Do / don’t

```text
✅ src/app/features/orders/pages/order-list/order-list.ts
✅ src/app/features/orders/orders.routes.ts

❌ src/app/order-list.ts  (feature UI at app root)
❌ src/app/random-service.ts  (belongs in core, shared, or a feature)
```

